## 11. Time and Space Complexity of K-Means

Let:
- \(n\) = Number of data points.
- \(k\) = Number of clusters.
- \(d\) = Number of features.
- \(i\) = Number of iterations.

### Time Complexity

\[
O(n \times k \times d \times i)
\]

This is because the algorithm calculates distances between data points and cluster centroids repeatedly.

### Space Complexity

\[
O(n \times d + k \times d)
\]

This accounts for storing the data and cluster centroids, excluding some implementation-specific overhead.

